        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "Partial demarcation and infarction of the upper pole of the spleen is not a rare occurrence after laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy (LSG). However, development of an abscess in the absence of leakage is extremely rare."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "CASE REPORTS",
          "content": "We present herein two unusual case reports of splenic abscess in patients following LSG."
        }
